/**
 * The three novenas that predate the per-group files.
 *
 * All three used to be generated by a `nineDays(theme)` string function that
 * emitted nine identical days ("Heavenly Father, on this Nth day of prayer…"),
 * published under `authorityLevel: "VATICAN"` against the bare roots
 * vatican.va and usccb.org. Nothing behind that text was received, and no page
 * was actually being cited. The template is gone.
 *
 * Two of the three now carry a received public-domain form, in the same shape
 * the group files use: the traditional novena prayer to the Sacred Heart
 * ("Divine Jesus, You have said, 'Ask and you shall receive…'", which recalls
 * the promises made to St Margaret Mary) repeated on each of the nine days,
 * and the nine distinct day-prayers of the traditional novena to St Theresa of
 * the Child Jesus. Both are reproduced from the cited page; nothing is
 * paraphrased or composed.
 *
 * The Divine Mercy novena is deliberately NOT reproduced. Its received daily
 * texts are Diary 1209-1229 of St Faustina Kowalska, and the English of them
 * in circulation is the Marian Fathers' 1987 translation, still under
 * copyright — the same reason `./novenas/group-1.ts` refuses to vendor the
 * USCCB Sacred Heart novena and `./prayers/batch-8.ts` gives the Divine Mercy
 * chaplet formulas without the Diary accounts around them. What is given here
 * is what is not anyone's expression: the nine daily intentions, stated in the
 * editors' own words, and the chaplet that is prayed for them on each day.
 * The Diary text is omitted rather than paraphrased.
 */

